#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124310 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32cbf366-20bd-5a52-a14f-83add698bf07" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Limit at Infinity: Rational Solutions"}] :question/id #uuid "0fc616fa-c901-53ff-acab-cdada6bb5ce2" :question/math-academy-id "e-80" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\infty} \\dfrac{3x^4+9x}{6x^4-x^3}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x^4$. Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\lim_{x \\to \\infty}\\frac{3x^{4} + 9x}{6x^{4} - x^{3}} &= \\lim_{x \\to \\infty}\\frac{(\\frac{3x^{4}}{x^{4}} + \\frac{9x}{x^{4}})}{(\\frac{6x^{4}}{x^{4}} - \\frac{x^{3}}{x^{4}})} \\\\\n&= \\lim_{x \\to \\infty}\\frac{(3 + \\frac{9}{x^{3}})}{(6 - \\frac{1}{x})} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3 + 0}{6 - 0} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124312 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "020c3de3-bcaf-5ade-ba50-2f15e344157d" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Limit at Infinity: Infinite Solutions"}] :question/id #uuid "b648ed80-e2e1-57c4-bd37-147d92315e90" :question/math-academy-id "e-81" :question/problem "Calculate $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow -\\infty} \\dfrac{4-5x-2x^3}{x^2+3}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x^2$. Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\lim_{x \\to - \\infty}\\frac{4 - 5x - 2x^{3}}{x^{2} + 3} &= \\lim_{x \\to - \\infty}\\frac{(\\frac{-2x^{3}}{x^{2}} - \\frac{5x}{x^{2}} + \\frac{4}{x^{2}})}{(\\frac{x^{2}}{x^{2}} + \\frac{3}{x^{2}})} \\\\\n&= \\lim_{x \\to - \\infty}\\frac{(-2x - \\frac{5}{x} + \\frac{4}{x^{2}})}{(1 + \\frac{3}{x^{2}})} \\\\\n&= \\lim_{x \\to - \\infty}(\\frac{-2x + 0 + 0}{1 + 0}) \\\\\n&= \\lim_{x \\to - \\infty}(-2x) \\\\\n&= \\infty\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124313 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee15db10-b92c-5f48-8983-e602068c7e08" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Horizontal Asymptote of a Rational Function"}] :question/id #uuid "c3798fe4-058f-5970-a903-65c654abb788" :question/math-academy-id "e-82" :question/problem "What is the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ with $f(x)=\\dfrac{2x^3+1}{x^3-15x}$?" :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is\n\n$$\ny=\\lim_{x \\rightarrow \\infty} f(x)\n$$\n\nTo find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x^3$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\lim_{x \\to \\infty}f(x) &= \\lim_{x \\to \\infty}\\frac{2x^{3} + 1}{x^{3} - 15x} \\\\\n&= \\lim_{x \\to \\infty}\\frac{(\\frac{2x^{3}}{x^{3}} + \\frac{1}{x^{3}})}{(\\frac{x^{3}}{x^{3}} - \\frac{15x}{x^{3}})} \\\\\n&= \\lim_{x \\to \\infty}\\frac{(2 + \\frac{1}{x^{3}})}{(1 - \\frac{15}{x^{2}})} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 + 0}{1 - 0} \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124326 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bde258b7-1654-5e73-8703-0e42371db8f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying When a Rational Function has No Horizontal Asymptote"}] :question/id #uuid "32a8e4bb-4191-55a8-883b-baa36f67b061" :question/math-academy-id "e-83" :question/problem "Find the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ where $f(x)=\\dfrac{x^5-10}{x^3-8x^2}$." :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is\n\n$$\ny=\\lim_{x \\rightarrow \\infty} f(x)\n$$\n\nTo find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x^3$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\lim_{x \\to \\infty}f(x) &= \\lim_{x \\to \\infty}\\frac{x^{5} - 10}{x^{3} - 8x^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\lim_{x \\to \\infty}\\frac{(\\frac{x^{5}}{x^{3}} - \\frac{10}{x^{3}})}{(\\frac{x^{3}}{x^{3}} - \\frac{8x^{2}}{x^{3}})} \\\\\n&= \\lim_{x \\to \\infty}\\frac{(x^{2} - \\frac{10}{x^{3}})}{(1 - \\frac{8}{x})} \\\\\n&= \\lim_{x \\to \\infty}(\\frac{x^{2} - 0}{1 - 0}) \\\\\n&= \\lim_{x \\to \\infty}x^{2} \\\\\n&= \\infty\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124827 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee15db10-b92c-5f48-8983-e602068c7e08" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Horizontal Asymptote of a Rational Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b092275-0441-51f6-a010-037dfba6f9f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121985} {:answer/id #uuid "97fada48-c296-548c-b940-338cfffbd117" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No horizontal asymptote" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121986} {:answer/id #uuid "e2569ab0-02c7-5ac5-b846-3a3d0cca1aa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121987} {:answer/id #uuid "01ab5ced-488e-53de-a635-3fb03079cdc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121988} {:answer/id #uuid "7f242d0b-0fd1-5380-b194-6c29749e0d9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01ab5ced-488e-53de-a635-3fb03079cdc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121988} :answer-field/id #uuid "17b4b97e-25e9-5c1e-b9ae-450448f2ae46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121984}] :question/id #uuid "24c1ddd3-5086-5a99-bc61-14c84e2545e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-35763" :question/problem "Find the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x) = \\frac{2x + 5}{2x^{3} + 2x + 6}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bde258b7-1654-5e73-8703-0e42371db8f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying When a Rational Function has No Horizontal Asymptote"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "853a1a88-bb31-595b-a05d-faec55e0de38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122045} {:answer/id #uuid "8bc1e936-5e6f-579a-b63b-656301cb3577" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122046} {:answer/id #uuid "9235c505-e485-526f-a286-a4e4a3a80ef0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122047} {:answer/id #uuid "11f32076-7fd0-5744-bc96-6b7297bc4538" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122048} {:answer/id #uuid "702f8245-c1b6-5ca6-b6e6-543e0e863129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No horizontal asymptote" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "702f8245-c1b6-5ca6-b6e6-543e0e863129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No horizontal asymptote" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122049} :answer-field/id #uuid "d30321be-736d-5b74-8428-7d00bbc108a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122044}] :question/id #uuid "d5a61e3c-7091-5d14-ae25-993daf76ef12" :question/math-academy-id "q-35834" :question/problem "Find the horizontal asymptote of $y = f(x)$ where $f(x) = \\frac{12x - 3x^{4}}{3x^{2} + 7}$."}]}
